{*
	Plan-choice modal (B4b + Phase 2) — included into both Upgrades/default.latte
	(matrix) and Upgrades/service.latte (per-service recipes). The operator picks
	one of two paths between the "Plan" click and the queue write:

	  (a) Migration in-place (default) → upgrades_planned.plan_mode='migration'
	  (b) Coexisting + data copy        → + a coexistence_planned track

	Option (b)'s radio is ENABLED only when the recipe declares
	coexistence_supported (the JS toggles it from data-coexist-supported on the
	triggering control). A single hidden CSRF <form> posts to Upgrades:planChoice;
	upgrades-plan-choice.js sets the hidden inputs + submits the real form (no
	fetch — preserving the redirect+flash UX). The <noscript> in-place fallback
	lives in the including templates, so a JS-off operator can still queue.

	Phase 2 — disruption preview + run_mode (see
	docs/plans/upgrade-reset-scope-and-session-safety.md §"Wing /upgrades surface",
	§"Run mode"). Above the rollout radios the modal renders the recipe's reset
	SCOPE as a human badge ("Container restart (~30s)" / "Stack bounce — N services
	(~90s)" / "Requires host reboot (~2 min)"). When the scope is session-risky
	(host_app / host_reboot — JS reads data-session-risk) the modal additionally
	shows a warning callout AND a run_mode radio group (Detached default /
	Attached, plus "Stage, then reboot" only for host_reboot). Non-session-risk
	recipes show the badge only — the hidden run_mode input stays 'attached', posted
	implicitly. The preview is JS-populated from data-* on the trigger button (same
	channel as data-coexist-supported); the partial is a static singleton.
*}
<div class="coex-modal-backdrop plan-choice-backdrop" id="plan-choice-modal" hidden
	 role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="plan-choice-title">
	<div class="coex-modal plan-choice-modal">
		<h3 id="plan-choice-title">Plan upgrade for <strong id="plan-choice-svc"></strong></h3>
		<p>
			Queue <strong id="plan-choice-recipe"></strong>. Pick how the new version
			rolls out — both paths only queue here; nothing applies until you run the
			matching tag.
		</p>

		<form method="post" id="plan-choice-form" action="" style="margin:0">
			<input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{$csrfToken}">
			<input type="hidden" name="plan_mode" id="plan-choice-mode" value="migration">
			<input type="hidden" name="target_version" id="plan-choice-target" value="">
			<input type="hidden" name="port_offset" id="plan-choice-port" value="100">
			<input type="hidden" name="data_copy" id="plan-choice-datacopy" value="1">
			<input type="hidden" name="run_mode" id="plan-choice-runmode" value="attached">

			{* Phase 2 disruption preview — JS fills #plan-choice-disruption-badge
			   (scope label + ~estimated_sec) from the trigger button's data-*; the
			   session-risk callout + run_mode fieldset are hidden until JS unhides
			   them for host_app / host_reboot scopes. *}
			<div class="plan-choice-disruption" id="plan-choice-disruption">
				<span class="plan-choice-disruption-label">Disruption</span>
				<span class="plan-choice-disruption-badge" id="plan-choice-disruption-badge"
					  data-scope="container"></span>
				<span class="plan-choice-disruption-detail" id="plan-choice-disruption-detail" hidden></span>
			</div>

			<div class="plan-choice-session-warning" id="plan-choice-session-warning" hidden role="alert">
				Applying this can disconnect your IDE / terminal session. Run it
				detached so the upgrade survives losing this connection.
			</div>

			<fieldset class="plan-choice-runmode" id="plan-choice-runmode-fieldset" hidden>
				<legend class="plan-choice-legend">Run mode</legend>

				<label class="plan-choice-option" data-runmode="detached">
					<input type="radio" name="plan_runmode_radio" value="detached" id="plan-choice-runmode-detached" checked>
					<span class="plan-choice-option-body">
						<span class="plan-choice-option-title">Detached (recommended)</span>
						<span class="plan-choice-option-desc">
							Hand the upgrade to the host runner and return immediately —
							it keeps going even if this session drops.
						</span>
					</span>
				</label>

				<label class="plan-choice-option" data-runmode="attached">
					<input type="radio" name="plan_runmode_radio" value="attached">
					<span class="plan-choice-option-body">
						<span class="plan-choice-option-title">Attached</span>
						<span class="plan-choice-option-desc">
							Stream the run in the foreground. If this session disconnects
							mid-apply the upgrade is interrupted.
						</span>
					</span>
				</label>

				{* Only meaningful for a host_reboot scope — JS unhides it just for
				   that case (a stack/container bounce never needs a reboot stage). *}
				<label class="plan-choice-option" id="plan-choice-runmode-stage-label"
					   data-runmode="stage_then_reboot" hidden>
					<input type="radio" name="plan_runmode_radio" value="stage_then_reboot" id="plan-choice-runmode-stage">
					<span class="plan-choice-option-body">
						<span class="plan-choice-option-title">Stage, then reboot</span>
						<span class="plan-choice-option-desc">
							Prepare everything now and reboot the host as the final step,
							so the disruptive change lands on a clean boot.
						</span>
					</span>
				</label>
			</fieldset>

			<fieldset class="plan-choice-options">
				<legend class="plan-choice-legend">Rollout path</legend>

				<label class="plan-choice-option" data-mode="migration">
					<input type="radio" name="plan_choice_radio" value="migration" checked>
					<span class="plan-choice-option-body">
						<span class="plan-choice-option-title">(a) Migration in-place</span>
						<span class="plan-choice-option-desc">
							Upgrade the running version directly. Applies under
							<code>ansible-playbook main.yml --tags upgrade</code>.
						</span>
					</span>
				</label>

				<label class="plan-choice-option" id="plan-choice-coexist-label" data-mode="coexist">
					<input type="radio" name="plan_choice_radio" value="coexist" id="plan-choice-coexist-radio">
					<span class="plan-choice-option-body">
						<span class="plan-choice-option-title">(b) Coexisting new version, with a copy of the data</span>
						<span class="plan-choice-option-desc">
							Boot the new version side-by-side on a shifted port, copy the data,
							then toggle it primary when ready. Needs a merged migration before
							it can provision.
						</span>
						<span class="plan-choice-coexist-na" hidden>
							This recipe does not support coexistence — only the in-place path is available.
						</span>
					</span>
				</label>
			</fieldset>
		</form>

		<div class="coex-modal-actions">
			<button type="button" class="mig-btn" data-action="close-plan-choice">Cancel</button>
			<button type="button" class="mig-btn mig-btn-primary" id="plan-choice-submit" data-action="submit-plan-choice">Queue plan</button>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
